meta {
  name: Check integrations compatibility
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opencti/integrations-compatibility?integration_versions=mitreattack@6.240930.0,crowdstrike@7.260309.0
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  integration_versions: mitreattack@6.240930.0,crowdstrike@7.260309.0
}

docs {
  Answers "are these integration versions compatible with OpenCTI?" for a
  batch of "slug@version" pairs. Public endpoint, no auth required.

  This is the inverse of the versions-matrix endpoint: the matrix answers
  "which version should I run?", this one verifies a version you already
  run.

  Without a `version` query param it checks against the latest registered
  OpenCTI version, echoed back as `opencti_version`.

  Swap the slugs/versions for ones that exist in your local instance — see
  the versions-matrix requests for the known list.

  Response shape:
  {
    "opencti_version": "7.260807.0",
    "integrations": [
      {
        "slug": "mitreattack",
        "integration_version": "6.240930.0",
        "compatible": true,
        "latest_compatible_integration_version": "6.240930.0"
      }
    ]
  }

  Entries come back in the order they were requested, one per requested
  pair, including duplicates.
}
